MiniCPM-o 4.5 single-GPU engine

The engine runs the MiniCPM-o 4.5 checkpoint (openbmb/MiniCPM-o-4_5, revision
503e754207c94da6bb26850b4469f367c9ea3582), whose weights, processor and model code
are licensed under Apache-2.0. The engine imports the checkpoint's processor and
encoder code. engine/models/multimodal.py contains an adapted copy of
MiniCPMWhisperEncoderLayer.forward for transformers 5.x. engine/runtime/track_s.py
ports MiniCPMO.streaming_generate and its chunked Talker generation
(modeling_minicpmo.py, utils.py) to the paged runtime.

The Token2Wav reference modules (stepaudio2: Token2wav, the CosyVoice2 flow and
HiFT) come from minicpmo-utils 1.0.6, Apache-2.0. engine/models/token2wav.py,
engine/runtime/token2wav_batch.py, engine/runtime/dit_fast.py and the graph
modules restructure that computation for batched, slot-cached and graph-captured
execution; they are tested against the reference modules.

FlashInfer, Triton and PyTorch provide GPU operators. No vLLM or SGLang engine,
scheduler or serving pipeline runs inside the engine. vLLM-Omni and SGLang-Omni
(Apache-2.0) are run unmodified as baselines from pinned checkouts; the speech
evaluation imports SGLang-Omni's Seed-TTS WER and speaker-similarity tools from
the pinned checkout. evals/speech/wavlm_blocked.py evaluates the attention of the
pinned WavLM scorer (s3prl) in query blocks over the same elements.

Model weights, datasets and evaluation audio are downloaded separately and are
not included in this repository. The Apache-2.0 text is in
third_party_licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.
